  {
    "id": "7c4b71005bec8cf13759d8a1",
    "path": "datafusion_expr_common::signature::Volatility::Stable",
    "name": "Stable",
    "owner": "datafusion_expr_common::signature::Volatility",
    "crate": "datafusion-expr-common",
    "version": "55.1.0",
    "kind": "variant",
    "signature": "Stable",
    "docs": "May return different values given the same input across different\nqueries but must return the same value for a given input within a query.\n\nFor example, the `now()` function is stable, because the query `select\ncol1, now() from t1`, will return different results each time it is run,\nbut within the same query, the output of the `now()` function has the\nsame value for each output row.\n\nDataFusion will inline `Stable` functions when possible. For example,\n`Stable` functions are inlined when planning a query for execution, but\nnot in View definitions or prepared statements.",
