  {
    "id": "c5fabfb9955a7015068c463b",
    "path": "datafusion_expr_common::signature::Volatility::Volatile",
    "name": "Volatile",
    "owner": "datafusion_expr_common::signature::Volatility",
    "crate": "datafusion-expr-common",
    "version": "55.1.0",
    "kind": "variant",
    "signature": "Volatile",
    "docs": "May change the return value from evaluation to evaluation.\n\nMultiple invocations of a volatile function may return different results\nwhen used in the same query on different rows. An example of this is the\n`random()` function.\n\nDataFusion can not evaluate such functions during planning or push these\npredicates into scans. In the query `select col1, random() from t1`,\n`random()` function will be evaluated for each output row, resulting in\na unique random value for each row.",
